soc: sunxi: h713-mips: restart the display MIPS from Linux, from a running core or out of the standby park

U-Boot loads display.bin once and starts the MIPS display core. Until
now, once the core was gone the picture was gone: a firmware that went
wrong cost a power cycle, and since the standby park (0208) a standby to
RAM cost a reboot. On the HY310 the restart was measured on 08.10.2026
with a test bench driver (V3, V8; V10 is on no record, doku/176). The core
was halted, display.bin was loaded again into the window U-Boot uses,
the core was started, cpu_comm reported it ready after 330 ms, the
receiver was bound again and the projected picture came back each time.
This driver repeats the sequences of that test bench, write for write:

 - from a running core (V3): the vendor's mips_reset() as 0167 did it.
   The bus, soft and cold resets go, the bus reset comes back, the gate
   is off around the cold reset, 20 us steps, the soft reset stays held
   (0x0200160c ends at 0x00030001). Then the load, then the vendor's
   start: boot address 0x4b100000, 20 us, 0x00070001.
 - out of the park (V8): the load, then U-Boot's h713_mips_release_reset():
   clock 0x80000002, resets 0, 0x10000, 0x30000, 0x30001 at 12 ms each,
   boot address, 0x00070001.
 - from a core held after a failed load: the load and the vendor start.
 - after a failed start: the park first, then as out of the park. That
   is V8 exactly as it ran, with its own halt.

The load is the vendor's load_data(): the code block up to the cfg file
(0xd01000) is zeroed, the image copied and compared, with the HDCP 1.4
key wait defused in it as U-Boot does at boot (one loop bound, refused
when there is none or there are two). Before every start
cpu_comm_firmware_reset() rebuilds cpu_comm's region with the core held.
After it cpu_comm_firmware_start() waits up to 10 s for READY. The file
is read and checked before anything is written; the soft reset must be
held before the window is written; the share registers and the boot
address are written only with the gate on and the bus reset released.

The driver is the one owner of the MIPS clock 0x02001600 and resets
0x0200160c (0230). It writes them raw, as U-Boot and the R1 park do; no
consumer of the clock framework's MIPS clocks and resets exists. cpu_comm
parks the core for standby through it, with the same writes as before.
Every register write is logged after its step with the value before and
the read-back, never between two writes of a timed sequence.

sysfs: "state" gives running, halted, parked or failed on its first line
and the four registers on the second; the MIPS block is not read with
the gate off. Writing a path to "restart" ("-" or nothing:
/boot/mips/display.bin) restarts the core and returns 0 or the error. A
failure leaves "halted" (core held, cpu_comm stopped) or "failed", says
why in a warning, and the next write starts over from there. The HDMI
receiver has to be unbound around it; h713-mips-restart does that.

Against the test bench three things differ on purpose. A failed region
rebuild keeps the core held, where the bench released it as 0167a did.
A halt or park that does not end in its register value stops the
restart. The state is read back from the registers instead of being
kept as phases across separate writes. The offline test, a register
model with the bench's sequences spelled literally (71 checks, 32 of 32
mutants caught), runs the driver source on the host.

Compiled out of tree against the R1 kernel with W=1, no warning. The
driver itself has not run on the device; what ran was the test bench
with the same sequences.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/Kconfig
@@ -61,3 +61,17 @@ config SUN50I_H713_TVCAP
 	  reflash, which is why the default is m.
 
 	  The module will be called sun50i-h713-tvcap.
+
+config SUN50I_H713_MIPS
+	tristate "Allwinner H713 display MIPS restart"
+	depends on ARCH_SUNXI || COMPILE_TEST
+	depends on OF && HY310_CPU_COMM
+	help
+	  Restarts the MIPS display core of the Allwinner H713 from Linux:
+	  loads display.bin again into the window U-Boot loaded it into and
+	  starts the core, from a running core or out of the standby park.
+	  It owns the core's clock and resets, and cpu_comm parks the core
+	  for a standby to RAM through it. One sysfs write; h713-mips-restart
+	  unbinds the HDMI receiver around it.
+
+	  The module will be called sun50i-h713-mips.
--- a/drivers/soc/sunxi/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/Makefile
@@ -4,3 +4,4 @@ obj-$(CONFIG_SUNXI_SRAM) +=	sunxi_sram.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_HY310_CPU_COMM) += cpu_comm/
 obj-$(CONFIG_SUN50I_H713_ARISC) += sun50i-h713-arisc.o
 obj-$(CONFIG_SUN50I_H713_TVCAP) += sun50i-h713-tvcap.o
+obj-$(CONFIG_SUN50I_H713_MIPS) += sun50i-h713-mips.o
--- /dev/null
+++ b/drivers/soc/sunxi/sun50i-h713-mips.c
@@ -0,0 +1,421 @@
+// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
+/*
+ * Allwinner H713: restart the MIPS display core from Linux, from a running
+ * core or out of the standby park. U-Boot loads display.bin once and starts
+ * the core; this driver loads the same file again into the window U-Boot
+ * used and starts it with the sequences that brought the picture back on
+ * the HY310 (08.10.2026, test bench h713-mips-test, V3/V8/V10):
+ *
+ *  running  -> halt as the vendor's mips_reset() (gate off around the cold
+ *              reset, 20 us steps, soft reset held), load, start as the
+ *              vendor's mipsloader ioctl (boot address, 20 us, released);
+ *  parked   -> load, start as U-Boot's h713_mips_release_reset() (clock
+ *              0x80000002, resets 0, 0x10000, 0x30000, 0x30001 at 12 ms,
+ *              boot address, released);
+ *  halted   -> load, vendor start;
+ *  failed   -> the standby park first, then as parked.
+ *
+ * It is the one owner of the MIPS clock 0x02001600 and resets 0x0200160c,
+ * written raw as U-Boot does (no consumer of the clock framework's MIPS
+ * clocks and resets exists): cpu_comm parks the core for standby through
+ * it. The MIPS block is read only with the gate on and the bus reset
+ * released. Every register write is logged after its step, with the value
+ * before and the read-back, never in the middle of a timed sequence.
+ *
+ * sysfs: "state" reads running|halted|parked|failed and a register line;
+ * writing a display.bin path ("-": /boot/mips/display.bin) to "restart"
+ * restarts the core. The receiver (sun50i-h713-hdmirx) has to be unbound
+ * around it: the restart rebuilds cpu_comm's region and everything the
+ * receiver told the old firmware is gone (h713-mips-restart does that).
+ */
+
+#include <linux/delay.h>
+#include <linux/io.h>
+#include <linux/kernel_read_file.h>
+#include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/mutex.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
+#include <linux/of_reserved_mem.h>
+#include <linux/platform_device.h>
+#include <linux/unaligned.h>
+#include <linux/vmalloc.h>
+#include <linux/soc/sunxi/h713-cpu-comm.h>
+
+#define H713_MIPS_CLK		0x0		/* 0x02001600, the core clock */
+#define H713_MIPS_RST		0xc		/* 0x0200160c: a set bit is released */
+#define H713_MIPS_GATE		0x00000001u	/* bus clock gate */
+#define H713_MIPS_BUS		0x00010000u
+#define H713_MIPS_COLD		0x00020000u
+#define H713_MIPS_SOFT		0x00040000u
+#define H713_MIPS_HELD		(H713_MIPS_GATE | H713_MIPS_BUS | H713_MIPS_COLD)
+#define H713_MIPS_RUN		(H713_MIPS_HELD | H713_MIPS_SOFT)	/* 0x00070001 */
+#define H713_MIPS_400MHZ	0x80000002u	/* gate on, M = 2 */
+#define H713_MIPS_STATUS	0x1c		/* bit 0: out of reset (1 in the soft reset too) */
+#define H713_MIPS_BOOTADDR	0x30
+#define H713_MIPS_WIN_BASE	0x4b100000	/* U-Boot's boot address */
+#define H713_MIPS_FW_MAX	0x00500000	/* U-Boot's image window */
+#define H713_MIPS_CFG_OFF	0x00d01000	/* cfg file, then TSE: kept */
+#define H713_MIPS_READY_MS	10000		/* U-Boot's budget */
+#define H713_MIPS_DEFAULT_FW	"/boot/mips/display.bin"
+/* "sltiu v1,v1,0x33" of Rx_HDCP14_LoadKey, with 0x06840093 built within 1 KiB */
+#define H713_HDCP_WAIT		0x2c630033
+#define H713_HDCP_NONE		0x2c630000
+#define H713_HDCP_CTX		0x400
+
+struct h713_mips_step { u8 reg; u32 keep, set; u16 us; };	/* reg = (reg & keep) | set */
+struct h713_mips_wlog { u32 reg, before, val, rb; };
+
+/* the vendor's mips_reset() from a running core; ends at 0x00030001 */
+static const struct h713_mips_step h713_mips_halt[] = {
+	{ H713_MIPS_RST, ~H713_MIPS_BUS, 0, 0 }, { H713_MIPS_RST, ~H713_MIPS_SOFT, 0, 0 },
+	{ H713_MIPS_RST, ~H713_MIPS_COLD, 0, 20 }, { H713_MIPS_RST, ~0u, H713_MIPS_BUS, 0 },
+	{ H713_MIPS_RST, ~H713_MIPS_GATE, 0, 20 }, { H713_MIPS_RST, ~0u, H713_MIPS_COLD, 20 },
+	{ H713_MIPS_RST, ~0u, H713_MIPS_GATE, 0 }, { 0xff }
+};
+
+/* the R1 standby park, U-Boot's h713_mips_stop() order */
+static const struct h713_mips_step h713_mips_park_seq[] = {
+	{ H713_MIPS_RST, 0, 0, 12000 }, { H713_MIPS_CLK, 0, 0, 12000 }, { 0xff }
+};
+
+/* U-Boot's h713_mips_release_reset() up to the boot address */
+static const struct h713_mips_step h713_mips_ladder[] = {
+	{ H713_MIPS_CLK, 0, H713_MIPS_400MHZ, 0 }, { H713_MIPS_RST, 0, 0, 12000 },
+	{ H713_MIPS_RST, 0, H713_MIPS_BUS, 12000 },
+	{ H713_MIPS_RST, 0, H713_MIPS_BUS | H713_MIPS_COLD, 12000 },
+	{ H713_MIPS_RST, 0, H713_MIPS_HELD, 12000 }, { 0xff }
+};
+
+enum h713_mips_state { H713_MIPS_RUNNING, H713_MIPS_HALTED, H713_MIPS_PARKED, H713_MIPS_FAILED };
+static const char * const h713_mips_state_name[] = { "running", "halted", "parked", "failed" };
+
+struct h713_mips {
+	struct device *dev;
+	void __iomem *regs, *ccu;
+	void *win;
+	phys_addr_t win_base;
+	struct mutex lock;		/* every register access after the probe */
+	enum h713_mips_state state;
+	struct cpu_comm_mips_owner owner;
+	struct h713_mips_wlog wlog[8];	/* writes not yet logged */
+	int nlog;
+};
+
+/* The writes of the step first, then its result; returns @err. */
+static __printf(3, 4) int h713_mips_say(struct h713_mips *m, int err, const char *fmt, ...)
+{
+	struct va_format vaf;
+	va_list ap;
+	int n;
+
+	for (n = 0; n < m->nlog; n++)
+		dev_info(m->dev, "0x%08x: 0x%08x -> 0x%08x, reads 0x%08x\n", m->wlog[n].reg,
+			 m->wlog[n].before, m->wlog[n].val, m->wlog[n].rb);
+	m->nlog = 0;
+	va_start(ap, fmt);
+	vaf.fmt = fmt;
+	vaf.va = &ap;
+	if (err)
+		dev_warn(m->dev, "%pV (%d), now %s\n", &vaf, err, h713_mips_state_name[m->state]);
+	else
+		dev_info(m->dev, "%pV\n", &vaf);
+	va_end(ap);
+	return err;
+}
+
+/* Logged by the next h713_mips_say(): a printk here would stretch the 20 us steps. */
+static void h713_mips_write(struct h713_mips *m, void __iomem *r, u32 reg, u32 val)
+{
+	u32 before = readl(r);
+
+	writel(val, r);
+	m->wlog[min(m->nlog, 7)] = (struct h713_mips_wlog){ reg, before, val, readl(r) };
+	m->nlog = min(m->nlog + 1, 8);	/* at most 7 writes between two lines */
+}
+
+static void h713_mips_steps(struct h713_mips *m, const struct h713_mips_step *s)
+{
+	for (; s->reg != 0xff; s++) {
+		h713_mips_write(m, m->ccu + s->reg, 0x02001600 + s->reg,
+				(readl(m->ccu + s->reg) & s->keep) | s->set);
+		wmb();	/* the write reaches the CCU before the wait starts */
+		fsleep(s->us);
+	}
+}
+
+static bool h713_mips_readable(struct h713_mips *m)
+{
+	u32 rst = readl(m->ccu + H713_MIPS_RST);
+
+	return (rst & (H713_MIPS_GATE | H713_MIPS_BUS)) == (H713_MIPS_GATE | H713_MIPS_BUS);
+}
+
+/* What the registers say; the status bit alone does not tell halted from running. */
+static enum h713_mips_state h713_mips_classify(struct h713_mips *m)
+{
+	u32 rst = readl(m->ccu + H713_MIPS_RST);
+
+	if ((rst & H713_MIPS_RUN) == H713_MIPS_RUN)
+		return (readl(m->regs + H713_MIPS_STATUS) & BIT(0)) ? H713_MIPS_RUNNING
+								   : H713_MIPS_FAILED;
+	if (rst == H713_MIPS_HELD)
+		return H713_MIPS_HALTED;
+	return rst ? H713_MIPS_FAILED : H713_MIPS_PARKED;
+}
+
+/* The one loop bound of the HDCP 1.4 key wait, defused as U-Boot does; 0: none or two. */
+static size_t h713_mips_defuse_hdcp_wait(u8 *img, size_t len)
+{
+	size_t p, q, found = 0;
+
+	for (p = 0; p + 4 <= len; p += 4) {
+		size_t to = min(p + H713_HDCP_CTX, len);
+		bool hi = false, lo = false;
+
+		if (get_unaligned_le32(img + p) != H713_HDCP_WAIT)
+			continue;
+		for (q = p > H713_HDCP_CTX ? p - H713_HDCP_CTX : 0; q + 2 <= to; q += 2) {
+			hi |= get_unaligned_le16(img + q) == 0x0684;
+			lo |= get_unaligned_le16(img + q) == 0x0093;
+		}
+		if (hi && lo && found)
+			return 0;
+		found = hi && lo ? p : found;
+	}
+	if (found)
+		put_unaligned_le32(H713_HDCP_NONE, img + found);
+	return found;
+}
+
+/* The vendor's load_data(): the code block zeroed, then copied, then compared. */
+static int h713_mips_load(struct h713_mips *m, const void *img, size_t n)
+{
+	if (readl(m->ccu + H713_MIPS_RST) & H713_MIPS_SOFT)
+		return h713_mips_say(m, -ENXIO, "load: the core is not held, window not written");
+	memset(m->win, 0, H713_MIPS_CFG_OFF);
+	memcpy(m->win, img, n);
+	wmb();	/* the image is in DRAM before the core can be released */
+	if (memcmp(m->win, img, n))
+		return h713_mips_say(m, -EIO, "load: window read-back differs, core held");
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static int h713_mips_start(struct h713_mips *m, bool uboot)
+{
+	const char *how = uboot ? "U-Boot" : "vendor";
+	int ret;
+
+	m->state = H713_MIPS_FAILED;	/* until the firmware says ready */
+	if (!uboot && readl(m->ccu + H713_MIPS_RST) != H713_MIPS_HELD)
+		return h713_mips_say(m, -ENXIO, "%s start: 0x0200160c 0x%08x, only from 0x00030001",
+				     how, readl(m->ccu + H713_MIPS_RST));
+	if (uboot)
+		h713_mips_steps(m, h713_mips_ladder);
+	/* the share registers and the boot address are in the MIPS block */
+	if (!h713_mips_readable(m))
+		return h713_mips_say(m, -ENXIO, "%s start: gate off or bus reset held", how);
+	ret = cpu_comm_firmware_reset();
+	if (ret)
+		return h713_mips_say(m, ret, "%s start: no new cpu_comm region, core held", how);
+	h713_mips_write(m, m->regs + H713_MIPS_BOOTADDR, 0x03061030, lower_32_bits(m->win_base));
+	wmb();	/* the boot address is set before the soft reset goes */
+	if (!uboot)
+		usleep_range(20, 25);
+	h713_mips_write(m, m->ccu + H713_MIPS_RST, 0x0200160c, H713_MIPS_RUN);
+	h713_mips_say(m, 0, "%s start: core released", how);
+	ret = cpu_comm_firmware_start(H713_MIPS_READY_MS);
+	if (!ret)
+		m->state = H713_MIPS_RUNNING;
+	return h713_mips_say(m, ret, "%s start: status 0x%08x, %sready", how,
+			     readl(m->regs + H713_MIPS_STATUS), ret ? "NOT " : "");
+}
+
+static int h713_mips_restart(struct h713_mips *m, const char *path)
+{
+	enum h713_mips_state from = m->state, regs = h713_mips_classify(m);
+	size_t size = 0, hdcp = 0;
+	void *img = NULL;
+	ssize_t n;
+	int ret;
+
+	n = kernel_read_file_from_path(path, 0, &img, H713_MIPS_FW_MAX, &size, READING_FIRMWARE);
+	if (n < 0)
+		return h713_mips_say(m, n, "restart: %s not read", path);
+	if (n >= SZ_64K && !(n & 3))
+		hdcp = h713_mips_defuse_hdcp_wait(img, n);
+	if (!hdcp) {
+		vfree(img);
+		return h713_mips_say(m, -EINVAL, "restart: %s, %zd bytes: %s", path, n,
+				     n < SZ_64K || (n & 3) ? "not the size of a display.bin"
+							   : "not exactly one HDCP wait site");
+	}
+	if (from != H713_MIPS_FAILED)
+		from = regs;	/* the registers are the owner's; they decide */
+	h713_mips_say(m, 0, "restart from %s: %s, %zd bytes, HDCP wait at 0x%zx",
+		      h713_mips_state_name[from], path, n, hdcp);
+	ret = cpu_comm_firmware_stop();
+	if (ret) {
+		h713_mips_say(m, ret, "restart: cpu_comm cannot stop, nothing written");
+		goto out;
+	}
+	if (from == H713_MIPS_RUNNING || from == H713_MIPS_FAILED) {
+		bool park = from == H713_MIPS_FAILED;	/* V8 with its halt, else V3 */
+		enum h713_mips_state want = park ? H713_MIPS_PARKED : H713_MIPS_HALTED;
+
+		h713_mips_steps(m, park ? h713_mips_park_seq : h713_mips_halt);
+		m->state = h713_mips_classify(m) == want ? want : H713_MIPS_FAILED;
+		ret = h713_mips_say(m, m->state == want ? 0 : -EIO,
+				    "%s: 0x02001600 0x%08x, 0x0200160c 0x%08x",
+				    park ? "park" : "vendor halt",
+				    readl(m->ccu + H713_MIPS_CLK), readl(m->ccu + H713_MIPS_RST));
+		if (ret)
+			goto out;
+	}
+	ret = h713_mips_load(m, img, n);
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = h713_mips_start(m, m->state != H713_MIPS_HALTED);
+out:
+	vfree(img);
+	return ret;
+}
+
+static ssize_t restart_store(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *attr,
+			     const char *buf, size_t count)
+{
+	struct h713_mips *m = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+	char path[128], *p;
+	int ret;
+
+	if (strscpy(path, buf, sizeof(path)) < 0)
+		return -ENAMETOOLONG;
+	p = strim(path);
+	mutex_lock(&m->lock);
+	ret = h713_mips_restart(m, *p && strcmp(p, "-") ? p : H713_MIPS_DEFAULT_FW);
+	mutex_unlock(&m->lock);
+	return ret ? ret : count;
+}
+static DEVICE_ATTR_WO(restart);
+
+static ssize_t state_show(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *attr, char *buf)
+{
+	struct h713_mips *m = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+	int len;
+
+	mutex_lock(&m->lock);
+	len = sysfs_emit(buf, "%s\n0x02001600=0x%08x 0x0200160c=0x%08x",
+			 h713_mips_state_name[m->state],
+			 readl(m->ccu + H713_MIPS_CLK), readl(m->ccu + H713_MIPS_RST));
+	if (h713_mips_readable(m))
+		len += sysfs_emit_at(buf, len, " 0x0306101c=0x%08x 0x03061030=0x%08x\n",
+				     readl(m->regs + H713_MIPS_STATUS),
+				     readl(m->regs + H713_MIPS_BOOTADDR));
+	else
+		len += sysfs_emit_at(buf, len, " 0x0306101c=not-read\n");
+	mutex_unlock(&m->lock);
+	return len;
+}
+static DEVICE_ATTR_RO(state);
+
+static struct attribute *h713_mips_attrs[] = { &dev_attr_restart.attr, &dev_attr_state.attr, NULL };
+ATTRIBUTE_GROUPS(h713_mips);
+
+/* cpu_comm asks: is there a core to park? Never reads the block with the gate off. */
+static bool h713_mips_alive(void *ctx)
+{
+	struct h713_mips *m = ctx;
+	bool alive;
+
+	mutex_lock(&m->lock);
+	alive = h713_mips_readable(m) && (readl(m->regs + H713_MIPS_STATUS) & BIT(0));
+	mutex_unlock(&m->lock);
+	return alive;
+}
+
+/* cpu_comm's standby park (suspend_late), after it closed the call path */
+static int h713_mips_park(void *ctx, u32 *clk, u32 *rst)
+{
+	struct h713_mips *m = ctx;
+	int ret;
+
+	mutex_lock(&m->lock);
+	h713_mips_steps(m, h713_mips_park_seq);
+	*clk = readl(m->ccu + H713_MIPS_CLK);
+	*rst = readl(m->ccu + H713_MIPS_RST);
+	ret = (*clk || *rst) ? -EIO : 0;
+	m->state = ret ? H713_MIPS_FAILED : H713_MIPS_PARKED;
+	h713_mips_say(m, ret, "park for standby: 0x02001600 0x%08x, 0x0200160c 0x%08x", *clk, *rst);
+	mutex_unlock(&m->lock);
+	return ret;
+}
+
+static void h713_mips_unown(void *ctx)
+{
+	struct h713_mips *m = ctx;
+
+	cpu_comm_set_mips_owner(NULL);
+	if (m->state != H713_MIPS_RUNNING)
+		dev_warn(m->dev, "unbound with the core %s: cpu_comm stays closed until a restart\n",
+			 h713_mips_state_name[m->state]);
+}
+
+static int h713_mips_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
+{
+	struct device *dev = &pdev->dev;
+	struct resource *res, win;
+	struct h713_mips *m;
+	int ret;
+
+	m = devm_kzalloc(dev, sizeof(*m), GFP_KERNEL);
+	if (!m)
+		return -ENOMEM;
+	m->dev = dev;
+	mutex_init(&m->lock);
+	m->regs = devm_platform_ioremap_resource(pdev, 0);
+	if (IS_ERR(m->regs))
+		return PTR_ERR(m->regs);
+	/* not requested: the CCU driver holds the region */
+	res = platform_get_resource(pdev, IORESOURCE_MEM, 1);
+	m->ccu = res && resource_size(res) >= 0x10 ? devm_ioremap(dev, res->start, 0x10) : NULL;
+	if (!m->ccu)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -ENODEV, "no MIPS clock and reset registers (reg 1)\n");
+	ret = of_reserved_mem_region_to_resource(dev->of_node, 0, &win);
+	if (ret || win.start != H713_MIPS_WIN_BASE || resource_size(&win) < H713_MIPS_CFG_OFF)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, -ENODEV, "no memory-region at 0x%x of 0x%x bytes\n",
+				     H713_MIPS_WIN_BASE, H713_MIPS_CFG_OFF);
+	m->win_base = win.start;
+	m->win = devm_memremap(dev, win.start, H713_MIPS_CFG_OFF, MEMREMAP_WC);
+	if (IS_ERR(m->win))
+		return PTR_ERR(m->win);
+	m->state = h713_mips_classify(m);
+	m->owner = (struct cpu_comm_mips_owner){ h713_mips_alive, h713_mips_park, m };
+	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, m);
+	ret = cpu_comm_set_mips_owner(&m->owner);
+	if (ret)
+		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret, "cpu_comm has another owner of the MIPS clock\n");
+	ret = devm_add_action_or_reset(dev, h713_mips_unown, m);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	return h713_mips_say(m, 0, "window 0x%llx+0x%x, 0x02001600 0x%08x, 0x0200160c 0x%08x, %s",
+			     (u64)m->win_base, H713_MIPS_CFG_OFF, readl(m->ccu + H713_MIPS_CLK),
+			     readl(m->ccu + H713_MIPS_RST), h713_mips_state_name[m->state]);
+}
+
+static const struct of_device_id h713_mips_of_match[] = {
+	{ .compatible = "allwinner,sun50i-h713-mips" },
+	{ }
+};
+MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, h713_mips_of_match);
+
+static struct platform_driver h713_mips_driver = {
+	.probe	= h713_mips_probe,
+	.driver	= {
+		.name		= "sun50i-h713-mips",
+		.of_match_table	= h713_mips_of_match,
+		.dev_groups	= h713_mips_groups,
+	},
+};
+module_platform_driver(h713_mips_driver);
+
